From 797180e4ae0ec0405f8084ceb3302a731dcd1e00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:45:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] qml: Write Buffer is a dropdown

Why: the Write Buffer choice was a header and two ActionTiles, Frames and
RAM, whose accent tone flipped like a radio button. Original Apertar shows
a choice of values as an InlineDropdownField with {value,label} options
(Compression, SettingsPage.qml:3244-3261@upstream-1.6.0, QML-23) and keeps
ActionTile for verbs with a fixed tone; no upstream QML file sets tone:
from a condition (QML-26).

What: in Settings > Record the header and the two tiles are one
InlineDropdownField "Write Buffer", value bridge bufferSetting, options
frames/Frames and ram/RAM, disabled while recording, onValueSelected
applyBufferMode(v). The wire form is unchanged (set_buffer_mode value=).
The Column, its visible: condition and the grey status text stay.

Tested: check_ui.sh lane-ui1 PASS (UI build, QML compiled ahead of time,
0 warnings). Not run on a screen. On the camera: cDNG or MLV, Settings >
Record, pick Write Buffer RAM, start and stop a take, then
  grep '^buffer=' ~/apertar-hardware.conf
shows ram; the field shows RAM, the status line under it follows, and the
field is greyed during the take.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NEFc1w7Y8dcyiV489BiwMr
---
 qml/SettingsPage.qml | 37 ++++++++++++-------------------------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

diff --git a/qml/SettingsPage.qml b/qml/SettingsPage.qml
index 3b5b2a8..a1f6853 100644
--- a/qml/SettingsPage.qml
+++ b/qml/SettingsPage.qml
@@ -3451,32 +3451,19 @@ Item {
                 visible: (root.cdngRecordFormat || root.recordFormat === "MLV")
                          && !!apertarControlBridge && apertarControlBridge.bufferSetting !== ""
 
-                Text {
-                    width: parent.width
-                    text: "Write Buffer"
-                    color: "white"
-                    font.pixelSize: 14
-                }
-
-                Row {
+                InlineDropdownField {
                     width: parent.width
-                    spacing: 12
-
-                    ActionTile {
-                        width: (parent.width - 12) / 2
-                        label: "Frames"
-                        tone: apertarControlBridge.bufferSetting === "frames" ? "accent" : "default"
-                        actionEnabled: !apertarControlBridge.recording
-                        onClicked: apertarControlBridge.applyBufferMode("frames")
-                    }
-
-                    ActionTile {
-                        width: (parent.width - 12) / 2
-                        label: "RAM"
-                        tone: apertarControlBridge.bufferSetting === "ram" ? "accent" : "default"
-                        actionEnabled: !apertarControlBridge.recording
-                        onClicked: apertarControlBridge.applyBufferMode("ram")
-                    }
+                    label: "Write Buffer"
+                    value: apertarControlBridge ? apertarControlBridge.bufferSetting : "frames"
+                    displayValue: value === "ram" ? "RAM" : "Frames"
+                    options: [
+                        { value: "frames", label: "Frames" },
+                        { value: "ram", label: "RAM" }
+                    ]
+                    fieldEnabled: apertarControlBridge && !apertarControlBridge.recording
+                    popupParent: dropdownOverlay
+                    dropdownController: sharedDropdownController
+                    onValueSelected: function(v) { apertarControlBridge.applyBufferMode(v) }
                 }
 
                 Text {
-- 
